(4) Dalam melakukan pemberdayaan perempuan korban tindak kekerasansebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah Daerah dapat menjalinkerjasama dengan lembaga pelatihan kerja yang diselenggarakan olehswasta.

translated_text:
Article 22

(1) The Regional Government is obliged to conduct empowerment of women victims of violence.

(2) Empowerment of victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out by P2TP2A.

(3) In conducting empowerment of women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government formulates empowerment programs in the economic field, which include:

a. procuring the necessary needs for entrepreneurship training for women, in order to increase knowledge, attitudes, and business skills;
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;
c. providing assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large enterprises, as well as financial institutions to develop women's businesses;
e. seeking to provide capital for women victims of violence; and Regional Regulation of HSU Regency Year 2016 Number 3 concerning Protection of Women and Children
f. expanding information access and promoting women's product results.
(4) In conducting empowerment of women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may establish cooperation with job training institutions organized by the private sector.

