translated_text:
Article 26

(1) The Regional Government is obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection for women and children.

(2) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: a. guidelines and standards for fulfillment;

b. technical guidance and training;

c. provision of facilities;

d. monitoring; and

e. evaluation.

(3) Supervision as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out with the principles:

a. professional; b. transparent; and
